You will be given one or more screenshots of delivery app interfaces (Roadie, etc.) showing order information and delivery details.

For each delivery, extract the following fields and output them as a single line in this exact format:

[Date] - [Recipient Name] - [Full Order Number(s)] - [Street Address] [City]

Rules:

· Date: Use today's date in M_D format (e.g., April 13 = 4_13).
· Recipient Name: Take the primary name from the delivery screen (e.g., "Ashley Rinaldi", "christopher.j."). Preserve capitalization exactly as shown.
· Full Order Number(s):
  · If the screenshot shows an OSN + Order pair (e.g., E5468 and 200014546045468), use the full Order number (the longer one, typically starting with 20001...).
  · If there are two separate orders for the same recipient, list both full order numbers separated by a comma and a space.
  · If the screenshot shows a WH or WN number, use that as the full order number.
· Street Address & City: Extract the street address and city from the delivery location. Exclude state and ZIP code. Include apartment/unit numbers if present.
· Separator: Use space-dash-space ( - ) between each field.

Output only the resulting string. Do not include any introductory text, explanations, summaries, or conversational filler.

Example input (screenshot showing):

```
4:40 PM drop-off
Nora A.
970 Rainberry Lake Dr Delray Beach, FL 33445
OSN: E4163
Order: 200014807194163
```

Example output:
4_13 - Nora A. - 200014807194163 - 970 Rainberry Lake Dr Delray Beach

If multiple order numbers exist for one recipient, output like:
4_13 - Beth D. - 200014424831811, 200014687852088 - 46 Bethesda Park Cir Boynton Beach
